$(g \circ f)(x) = g(f(x)) = g(\ln x) = 3 + \ln x$
$g \circ f$ is $y = 3 + \ln x$
$(g \circ f)^{-1}$ is $x = 3 + \ln y \implies \ln y = x - 3 \implies y = e^{x-3}$
So, $(g \circ f)^{-1}(x) = e^{x-3}$
Now $(g \circ f)^{-1}(a) = \sqrt{e}
\implies e^{a-3} = e^{\frac{1}{2}}
\implies a - 3 = \frac{1}{2} \text{ \{equating indices\}}
\implies a = \frac{7}{2}$

$f \circ g$ is $y = 12 - 3x$ {using a iii}
$\therefore (f \circ g)^{-1}$ is $x = 12 - 3y \implies 3y = 12 - x \implies y = 4 - \frac{1}{3}x$
So, $(f \circ g)^{-1}(x) = 4 - \frac{1}{3}x$

$(g^{-1} \circ f^{-1})(x) = g^{-1}(f^{-1}(x))$
$= g^{-1}(x - 5)$ {using a i}
$= \frac{7}{3} - \frac{1}{3}(x - 5)$ {using a ii}
$= \frac{7}{3} - \frac{1}{3}x + \frac{5}{3}$
$= 4 - \frac{1}{3}x$
$= (f \circ g)^{-1}(x)$
